@packages/core/src/model/language.sigil from SigilLanguageModel import { LanguageModel }
@packages/core/src/model/diagnostics.sigil from SigilDiagnosticModel import { DiagnosticModel }

component SigilSourceModel {
  goal {
    Define recovered Sigil source documents, Facets, and declarations for
    parsers and deterministic consumers.
  }

  interface {
    SourceModel {
      LanguageModel supplies structural vocabulary and source positions, and
      DiagnosticModel supplies diagnostics. Facet, EmbeddedFacet, EmbeddedContent,
      sections, components, SigilDocument, ParseResult, FormatResult, and
      ParseOptions preserve recovered source structures and diagnostics.

      A Facet preserves its introducing prose, source location, component owner,
      contract role, optional local grouping Tag occurrence, and one attached
      payload when present. An EmbeddedFacet is the complete Facet with attached
      fenced content, including an empty payload, not the fenced body alone.

      isEmbeddedFacet identifies the attached-payload form. Existing units and
      literalBlocks serialized field names remain stable where compatible with
      the explicit 0.8 structures and the schema-2 native frontend boundary.

      Component is the ownership container. A contract can freely mix direct
      Facets and multiple local grouping occurrences; an ungrouped Facet needs no
      synthetic wrapper identity.

      Type documentation encourages Tags for useful recurring identities and
      grouping where it connects contributions, preserving direct shared
      guarantees and small components without redundant groups.

      Source documents retain exact original text, raw bytes for disk inputs,
      physical line endings, BOM, and a common source map. String overlays are
      validated as scalar sequences before deriving UTF-8 offsets; their encoded
      bytes are not evidence about any original disk encoding.

      First-class inline Tag introductions, local grouping occurrences, import
      selections, eligible bare references, and complete links remain distinct
      records with exact spelling, original ranges, and relevant Facet ownership.
      No expand form, visibility layer, or single-Concept field survives in the
      0.8 source contract.

      Links retain raw spans, labels, destinations, titles, and image kind;
      payloads retain original lines, delimiter ranges, and dedented presentation
      separately. Parsing content does not retrieve link targets.

      Recovered structures retain validity and completeness evidence and never
      expose invented definitions as valid authored declarations. Scanner records
      retain candidates separately from later collective owner and Tag resolution.
    }
  }
}
